WEBVTT

00:35.246 --> 00:37.623
<i>Tuesday on
Scarecrow and Mrs. King.</i>

00:37.706 --> 00:40.584
<i>My God, what did those
drug dealers do to you?</i>

00:40.710 --> 00:42.835
<i>Oh, they took my chest out
and threw it over there.</i>

00:42.918 --> 00:45.338
<i>Then they pulled my legs out
and threw them over there.</i>

00:45.421 --> 00:49.299
Brian, you're still watching TV?
God, you've been sitting there since I left.

00:49.382 --> 00:53.345
Yeah. I spent all morning watching
a VH1 special on Gwen Stefani.

00:53.553 --> 00:57.723
I don't know what a "hollaback girl" is.
All I know is I want her dead.

00:57.847 --> 00:59.140
Hey, can you hand me the remote?

00:59.224 --> 01:02.018
You know, you've been laying
around the house a lot lately.

01:02.143 --> 01:04.686
Why don't you get a part-time job
like Peter used to have?

01:49.223 --> 01:53.560
Mom, guess what? I just found out I got
that internship at Mayor West's office.

01:53.644 --> 01:56.103
Wow, congratulations, Meg.

01:56.186 --> 01:59.231
Yeah, it was a really tough interview,
but I totally nailed it.

01:59.524 --> 02:02.942
All right, Meg, we're going to start
with a little word association.

02:03.068 --> 02:05.862
I'll say a word, and you say
whatever comes into your head.

02:05.946 --> 02:07.071
- Okay.
- Mosquito.

02:07.196 --> 02:08.739
- Bite.
- Bite.

02:08.822 --> 02:10.281
- Mosquito.
- Yes. Good one.

02:10.364 --> 02:11.409
- Mosquito.
- Bite.

02:11.533 --> 02:12.576
- Mosquito.
- Bite.

02:12.701 --> 02:13.659
- Mosquito.
- Bite.

02:13.784 --> 02:15.119
- Bite.
- Mosquito.

02:15.452 --> 02:18.789
Very good.
You are a worthy opponent, indeed.

02:19.039 --> 02:20.791
Congratulations. You're hired.

02:20.916 --> 02:24.209
Your first job is to go down to the corner
and tell that hobo

02:24.293 --> 02:26.086
I admire his spirit.

02:26.212 --> 02:28.338
I'm too self-conscious to do it.

02:28.671 --> 02:30.924
Honey, I'm so proud of you.

02:31.050 --> 02:35.136
- You see, Brian, Meg has a job.
- Hey, Meg, if you're working for the Mayor,

02:35.261 --> 02:39.055
you know what that means?
Even you're doing better than Brian.

02:39.555 --> 02:42.265
Hey, everybody, Brian's the new Meg.

02:44.602 --> 02:48.022
Brian's the new Meg. Brian's the new Meg.

02:48.147 --> 02:50.650
- Yeah, you're the new me.
- Shut up, Meg.

02:54.943 --> 02:57.028
Let's go, kids. Time for school.

02:57.154 --> 03:00.698
Lois, I don't want to ruin your morning,
but I flushed a diaper.

03:00.823 --> 03:01.783
It's a mess up there.

03:03.952 --> 03:07.037
Brian, what is this? You're driving a cab?

03:07.161 --> 03:10.831
Well, Lois, I realized you were right.
I mean, it's time I went out and got a job.

03:10.957 --> 03:12.750
For God sakes, I'm seven years old.

03:12.833 --> 03:16.169
Seven? That's not bad.
You know, Todd was 15 when he died.

03:16.294 --> 03:17.463
The dog we had before you.

03:17.796 --> 03:19.630
Hey, Peter, did you call me?

03:19.714 --> 03:21.589
Yeah, I thought we'd go to the park, Todd.

03:21.672 --> 03:24.217
You're not taking me to the vet, are you?

03:24.342 --> 03:26.343
No, no, just a nice day at the park.

03:26.469 --> 03:29.346
I'm a little worried that
you're gonna have me put down.

03:29.430 --> 03:33.517
I know there's been some concern
about my sphincter's low shutter speed.

03:33.642 --> 03:35.476
No, no, we're just going to the park, Todd.

03:35.559 --> 03:38.229
Okay, well, I'll enjoy the ride, then.

03:40.438 --> 03:42.565
Around the park
one more time, Bitterman.

03:42.691 --> 03:43.860
Peter, I'm not your chauffeur.

03:43.984 --> 03:45.986
Not for long with that attitude, Bitterman.

03:47.195 --> 03:48.612
This is living, Bitterman.

03:48.695 --> 03:52.157
This set of wheels is even better than
those talking cars on that commercial.

03:53.032 --> 03:54.492
Hey, how you doing there?

03:54.575 --> 03:58.412
Listen, I couldn't help but notice
you across the parking lot and...

03:59.164 --> 04:01.707
You know, you're very attractive and...

04:01.832 --> 04:04.334
You want to go behind the Applebee's
and do it?

04:04.417 --> 04:08.502
You want to just go have some dirty,
stupid, insane parking-lot sex?

04:08.795 --> 04:12.089
- Chuck, it's me, Morty.
- Yeah, 'cause we could... What?

04:12.382 --> 04:16.801
- Yeah, they had me painted.
- Oh, my God, I'm so embarrassed.

04:16.885 --> 04:17.970
- Oh, my...
- Hey, how do you think I feel?

04:18.052 --> 04:20.346
- No, no, that, too, but...
- It's not all about you, you know.

04:20.430 --> 04:22.056
Morty, oh, my God, what are you doing?
Look at you.

04:22.181 --> 04:24.850
Think I was like a birthday present
for the kid or something like that.

04:24.975 --> 04:27.268
Oh, my God, look at you. You're hot.

04:27.393 --> 04:28.520
- I know.
- I would've taken you...

04:28.646 --> 04:30.021
You know what I would've
done to you back there?

04:30.105 --> 04:31.480
- Yeah?
- Why didn't you say something earlier?

04:31.564 --> 04:34.149
- I said all that stuff. God!
- Let's not rule anything out.

04:37.068 --> 04:38.904
- Hey, look, there's Lois.
- Yeah.

04:39.029 --> 04:39.987
Hey, honk the horn.

04:42.323 --> 04:43.532
Hi, Peter.

04:44.242 --> 04:45.366
- Ram her.
- What?

04:45.491 --> 04:48.244
- I said ram her!
- What the hell?

04:48.411 --> 04:49.704
- Now shoot her tires out.
- What?

04:49.829 --> 04:51.038
- You got a gun?
- Well, yeah.

04:51.163 --> 04:53.873
- Every cabbie carries a gun, but...
- Give me the gun.

04:59.546 --> 05:02.590
What the hell is wrong with you, Peter?
You could've killed me!

05:02.715 --> 05:06.217
Yeah, but I got you good, Lois. Admit it.
Just say it, I got you.

05:08.387 --> 05:10.346
All right, you got me.

05:11.555 --> 05:13.848
- I told you.
- Oh, my God.

05:14.389 --> 05:17.518
- Oh, no, what happened here?
- We got into a little accident.

05:17.601 --> 05:19.102
- It's all right.
- Oh, no.

05:19.228 --> 05:22.231
Well, I guess accidents happen
when you least expect them.

05:22.356 --> 05:24.941
That's how come they call them accidents.

05:25.066 --> 05:28.945
Look, you got the community events
corkboard wedged in your grill.

05:29.236 --> 05:30.444
There, that's better.

05:30.570 --> 05:34.574
Don't you all forget to sign up for
the Quahog Community Talent Show.

05:34.700 --> 05:37.785
Talent show? Peter, that could be fun.

05:37.951 --> 05:39.661
Do you think we have
a chance at winning?

05:39.786 --> 05:41.914
Absolutely. I love being around the stage.

05:41.998 --> 05:44.207
<i>Except for that time we went to see
Phantom of the Opera.</i>

05:50.128 --> 05:53.589
Let's see the gross
half of your face! Come on!

05:53.714 --> 05:57.132
Let's see the gross half of your face
so I can get out of here!

05:57.216 --> 05:59.051
- That nose better be piggy.
- Shut up.

05:59.135 --> 06:00.135
You shut up.

06:16.399 --> 06:19.694
Oh, your old guitar.
I haven't seen that thing in ages.

06:19.819 --> 06:22.780
Well, Lois, I thought you and me could
do a song for the talent show.

06:22.864 --> 06:25.406
It could be just like the old days
when we used to play.

06:25.490 --> 06:29.202
You remember, Lois?
Remember our band, Handful of Peter?

06:29.452 --> 06:32.329
Hi, there. I'm Peter, and this is Lois.

06:32.413 --> 06:34.457
We want to talk to you
about a friend of ours.

06:34.582 --> 06:35.999
He's not here tonight.

06:36.124 --> 06:38.168
Although, you know,
he's kind of here, Lois.

06:38.292 --> 06:41.586
- You know, you're right. He kind of is.
- Yeah, because he's in our hearts.

06:41.670 --> 06:45.257
This is a song about that man
and his world

06:45.339 --> 06:47.091
that was taken from him.

07:37.549 --> 07:41.010
- They're gone now.
- How could this have happened?

07:41.094 --> 07:42.302
- How?
- How?

07:42.554 --> 07:45.054
I haven't thought about that in years.

07:45.181 --> 07:47.349
You know, it would be fun
to write some new songs.

07:47.433 --> 07:49.934
<i>You know what else is fun?
Watching Mr. Belvedere</i>

07:50.060 --> 07:52.143
without people talking so loud.

07:52.310 --> 07:53.729
So I was thinking we could...

08:06.072 --> 08:08.657
Hello. Hey, Lois, what's up?

08:08.783 --> 08:11.618
Milk? Yeah, I'll pick some up
at the end of my shift.

08:11.743 --> 08:14.371
Gotta go. First fare of the night.

08:16.707 --> 08:19.667
I should really pick up
that milk now before I forget.

08:20.917 --> 08:22.836
You son of a bitch!

08:25.255 --> 08:28.382
Hey, Brian, you see that magazine
cover right there? See who's on it?

08:28.508 --> 08:31.551
- Yeah, that's Jessica Alba.
- Yeah, you want to know a secret, buddy?

08:31.635 --> 08:32.971
- What?
- I would do her.

08:33.095 --> 08:34.262
- Really?
- Oh, yeah.

08:34.386 --> 08:37.639
I just wanted you to know a little bit
about who I am.

08:37.765 --> 08:39.058
Thanks for the milk, Carl.

08:40.393 --> 08:43.395
What the hell? $400?

08:43.603 --> 08:47.357
<i>My God, this is a bigger ripoff than
Peter's Sounds of the Rainforest CD.</i>

08:47.773 --> 08:50.149
This will help us fall asleep, Lois.

09:05.996 --> 09:08.331
<i>All right,
let's get rid of all these trees.</i>

09:08.457 --> 09:11.459
<i>Once they're gone, this'll be
a great place to raise cheap beef.</i>

09:11.585 --> 09:13.753
<i>- Up yours, Sting!
- Yeah, yeah!</i>

09:13.877 --> 09:15.629
<i>Hey, what's that song he does that I hate?</i>

09:15.754 --> 09:18.882
<i>- Desert Rose.
- Yeah, yeah, that song sucks.</i>

09:22.217 --> 09:24.928
Meg, I'm going to lunch now,
and I'm having pizza.

09:25.013 --> 09:29.640
So if you see the Noid running around,
tell him if he ruins my pizza's freshness,

09:29.765 --> 09:31.559
I'll snap his neck.

09:33.852 --> 09:37.271
Hey, Meg, I need to see the Mayor
about this $400 parking ticket.

09:37.355 --> 09:40.983
Brian, you can't just barge in here.
You have to make an appointment.

09:41.109 --> 09:42.943
But this is flat-out extortion.

09:43.026 --> 09:46.530
No, it's not. Adam can charge
whatever he wants for a parking ticket.

09:46.655 --> 09:48.613
You know, Meg,
that guy's been playing fast and loose

09:48.698 --> 09:50.699
with his position for years now,
and I've had it.

09:50.825 --> 09:53.451
- He's a corrupt bastard.
- That is not true.

09:53.535 --> 09:54.537
Yes, it is.

09:54.661 --> 09:57.540
Somebody's got to stand up
and prove to this town that he's a crook.

09:57.664 --> 09:59.749
And it looks like it has to be me.

10:00.707 --> 10:02.125
What was all the commotion?

10:02.209 --> 10:03.542
Nothing, it was just...

10:24.102 --> 10:27.479
Perhaps it was the Noid
who should've avoided me.

10:34.277 --> 10:35.818
You know what, Brian?

10:35.902 --> 10:38.698
It took me two hours to spell "hat"
with these things.

10:38.822 --> 10:42.325
I finally got the "T" right side up,
and then you come in here...

10:42.782 --> 10:45.286
You're a bastard. Where are you going?

10:45.369 --> 10:48.912
I'm going to expose Mayor West
as the corrupt politician that he is.

10:49.038 --> 10:51.750
I'm on my way to meet a source
who won't talk to me over the phone.

10:51.876 --> 10:54.043
Scandal in Quahog. Count me in.

10:56.713 --> 10:58.962
Oh, my God, speed up, speed up, speed up.

11:00.089 --> 11:03.676
There you are, you honky son of a bitch,
come back here.

11:10.390 --> 11:12.057
Thank you for coming, Deep Throat.

11:12.182 --> 11:14.475
You'll understand if I don't come out
from the shadows.

11:14.559 --> 11:17.437
My identity will be safest
if you never see my face.

11:17.562 --> 11:18.688
Okay.

11:18.813 --> 11:21.524
Mayor West hasn't slept at home
for three nights.

11:21.649 --> 11:23.192
Kermit the Frog?

11:23.651 --> 11:26.235
Somebody talked! No one is safe!
I'm getting out of here!

11:28.237 --> 11:29.573
What's his appeal?

11:42.207 --> 11:43.666
Well, that wasn't very good.

11:43.791 --> 11:45.876
We're never gonna win that talent show.

11:46.001 --> 11:49.213
Hey, now, Peter, you gotta remember
that when we used to write the old songs,

11:49.339 --> 11:51.882
we had a lot of "inspiration," huh?

11:52.717 --> 11:56.927
You know, I think Brian may have some
inspiration in a cigar box under his bed.

11:57.052 --> 11:59.512
I don't know, Lois.
I don't think this is gonna work.

11:59.596 --> 12:01.722
Come on, we can't give up on our goals.

12:01.848 --> 12:03.433
What if Jesus had done that?

12:08.562 --> 12:11.064
Why is the ironing board still out?

12:13.316 --> 12:18.111
That's my favorite picture
of Brian over there on that wall.

12:18.361 --> 12:22.116
He wants to have sex with me so bad.

12:25.408 --> 12:26.368
He's not...

12:26.618 --> 12:29.163
He's not gonna get to.

12:38.378 --> 12:40.588
All right. There he goes. Let's move.

12:42.423 --> 12:44.132
I say, what are we looking for?

12:44.257 --> 12:46.551
I don't know, some proof
of Mayor West's corruption.

12:47.469 --> 12:49.887
Whoa, whoa,
what the hell are you guys doing here?

12:49.971 --> 12:52.765
I'm sorry.
We happen to be here to solve a case.

12:52.848 --> 12:54.850
- We were here first.
- Well,

12:54.975 --> 12:58.269
you know, this is a free country, dude,
and we are here to go to work.

12:58.395 --> 13:00.104
Free country, but this is our beat,
you know?

13:00.187 --> 13:01.481
Yeah, but we are here to go to work.

13:01.607 --> 13:03.316
We've been called,
and that's why we're here.

13:03.441 --> 13:04.400
You know what? I tell you.

13:04.483 --> 13:06.067
How about you just turn around
and walk away?

13:06.150 --> 13:07.943
- No, I don't think so.
- Hey, you know what...

13:08.027 --> 13:10.945
- We do not walk away.
- I'll get you started.

13:19.579 --> 13:22.705
What are you doing here, Brian?
Still trying to smear my boss?

13:22.831 --> 13:27.001
No, no, no. I actually came to my senses
and realized I was out of line.

13:27.126 --> 13:29.170
I'm just here to apologize.

13:29.837 --> 13:33.756
Oh, and you're so pretty.

13:34.716 --> 13:39.219
- You're always pretty.
- You guys are so sweet.

13:39.844 --> 13:43.390
- Well, it's my pleasure.
- Hey, can you guys hold on a sec?

13:43.515 --> 13:46.642
- I gotta get this to Helen in Accounting.
- Okay, bye.

13:50.144 --> 13:51.104
Aha!

13:51.229 --> 13:54.149
The Mayor's datebook.
This should tell us what we wanna know.

13:54.232 --> 13:55.649
All right, let's get out of here.

13:55.732 --> 13:58.735
Oh, God, I feel more delirious
than my cousin, Stewie Cruise.

13:58.903 --> 14:01.780
I'm in love with Katie Holmes!
I'm in love with Katie Holmes!

14:01.864 --> 14:04.364
I'm not gay! Go see my new movie!

14:04.490 --> 14:06.742
I'm in love with Katie Holmes! I'm not gay!

14:08.785 --> 14:13.330
All we need is one incriminating entry
in this datebook, and that's our ticket to...

14:13.539 --> 14:16.124
Hey, Brian. What's up?

14:17.125 --> 14:19.586
Hi, Lois, Peter.

14:19.710 --> 14:23.047
Brian, did you know this couch was here?

14:23.213 --> 14:25.840
It's so comfortable.

14:25.924 --> 14:28.677
Hey, Lois, look how short Stewie is.

14:29.552 --> 14:31.469
He's so short.

14:33.013 --> 14:35.557
Oh, my God. He is short.

14:40.728 --> 14:41.687
Hey.

14:42.020 --> 14:43.439
Hey, Brian.

14:43.981 --> 14:46.524
He's knocking on the back door.

14:46.858 --> 14:48.527
What should I do?

14:48.609 --> 14:49.652
What?

14:49.735 --> 14:52.528
He's knocking on the back door.

14:52.612 --> 14:54.198
Should I let him in?

14:54.323 --> 14:55.865
I'm scared.

14:55.949 --> 14:58.200
Well, you two are busy being nude.

14:58.325 --> 15:02.245
So, we'll just head out and

15:03.037 --> 15:05.205
let you be nude.

15:05.998 --> 15:10.043
- Who were those guys?
- I don't know.

15:10.127 --> 15:11.753
Room for one more?

15:15.923 --> 15:18.300
Well, this is the last entry in the datebook.

15:18.424 --> 15:22.011
"Super secret meeting at motel.
Inform no one. "

15:22.137 --> 15:23.430
I think we got him now.

15:23.555 --> 15:25.556
You know, you really shouldn't
lie on that bedspread.

15:25.682 --> 15:29.100
I saw this report on TV
about how filthy hotel rooms are.

15:29.184 --> 15:31.019
<i>In a moment, we will use the special lights</i>

15:31.102 --> 15:35.105
<i>to see just how filthy
this seemingly clean hotel room really is.</i>

15:41.278 --> 15:43.111
Well? What do you see?

15:45.697 --> 15:49.242
Oh, Jem, you are truly outrageous.

15:49.368 --> 15:51.828
Truly, truly, truly outrageous.

15:52.287 --> 15:55.081
I see a grown man enjoying cartoons.

15:56.123 --> 16:00.251
Well, that's it, then. The only thing
this guy is guilty of is being a whack job.

16:00.335 --> 16:02.420
Wait, wait, wait. Somebody's coming in.

16:02.545 --> 16:04.087
It's just some fat hooker.

16:04.630 --> 16:07.800
- Oh, my God, it's Meg!
- What?

16:07.924 --> 16:09.927
Meg and Adam West. Ew!

16:11.176 --> 16:12.637
Sorry, sorry.

16:18.767 --> 16:20.352
God, this is incredible.

16:20.477 --> 16:23.563
The Mayor is dating a teenage intern,
and it's Meg.

16:23.645 --> 16:24.771
What a story.

16:24.896 --> 16:27.023
This is the perfect scandal
to take him down.

16:27.147 --> 16:30.442
- All we need is taped evidence.
- Well, I've got the disguises right here.

16:32.902 --> 16:35.655
I thought you were supposed
to get the suit and the top hat.

16:35.780 --> 16:36.740
I liked this one better.

16:36.864 --> 16:38.826
Anything to wear a dress, huh?

16:42.118 --> 16:44.286
Gosh, you're swell, Meg.

16:44.412 --> 16:46.497
I really have a great time
when I'm with you.

16:46.622 --> 16:49.292
Mayor West, I feel exactly the same way.

16:49.417 --> 16:51.793
Please, please. Call me Mayor ChapStick.

16:52.670 --> 16:54.921
Well, we should probably go.

16:55.004 --> 16:57.004
Here they come. Kiss me.

16:59.341 --> 17:01.218
Come on, we gotta follow them.

17:02.010 --> 17:02.969
Stewie?

17:03.094 --> 17:04.387
Huh? Oh. Oh.

17:04.512 --> 17:06.431
- Everything all right?
- Yeah.

17:06.514 --> 17:07.514
Uh...

17:07.808 --> 17:09.807
Hey, listen, freaking shot in the dark.

17:09.932 --> 17:11.476
You wanna do something sometime?

17:14.687 --> 17:18.691
Great practice, Lois.
We are totally ready for that talent show.

17:18.857 --> 17:21.610
Oh, my God, Peter, I am so wasted.

17:21.735 --> 17:25.321
All I want to do is make cookies.
Oh, my God, I have a great idea.

17:25.403 --> 17:27.906
- Let's make cookies.
- We don't have to, Lois.

17:28.030 --> 17:31.660
Look, there's a magical land
of desserts right behind you.

17:44.419 --> 17:46.671
Help! Stop!

17:52.385 --> 17:56.220
- Oh, Brian. You scared me.
- Another late night, huh?

17:56.429 --> 18:00.224
- Yeah, Mayor West keeps me pretty busy.
- Yeah, I noticed.

18:02.350 --> 18:03.686
Where did you get that?

18:03.770 --> 18:05.728
Meg, what the hell
have you gotten yourself into?

18:05.853 --> 18:08.147
You realize he probably does this
with every new intern.

18:08.231 --> 18:10.524
That's not true. Adam and I are in love.

18:10.649 --> 18:14.819
Don't be ridiculous. Listen,
I'm warning you because I care about you.

18:14.903 --> 18:16.655
I am going to the press with this story,

18:16.738 --> 18:20.157
and when it hits,
it'll be bigger than Uncle Sam's nipples.

18:20.907 --> 18:24.536
- Jeez! What the hell?
- They're called nipples, guys.

18:24.619 --> 18:26.036
They're freaking huge.

18:26.120 --> 18:28.996
You know what? Maybe we can just
all relax and enjoy the sauna.

18:35.752 --> 18:38.881
- I have to tell you something, Adam.
- You're an alien. I know.

18:39.006 --> 18:43.218
No, no, my dog is gonna expose
our relationship to the press.

18:43.302 --> 18:44.552
Well, so what?

18:47.096 --> 18:50.766
I told you that I'd wait for you
until you're 18 or 21.

18:50.890 --> 18:53.351
Or maybe 25,
when you can legally rent a car.

18:53.435 --> 18:54.434
They don't care.

18:54.560 --> 18:56.396
They're gonna make you
look like a monster.

18:56.479 --> 18:57.479
I see.

18:57.604 --> 19:00.858
Well, Meg, I'm a public figure.
I'm used to the tabloids' doodie.

19:00.940 --> 19:02.358
It's you I'm worried about.

19:02.441 --> 19:05.735
You're just a sweet young lady
with her whole life ahead of her.

19:05.818 --> 19:09.573
This story could ruin your future,
and I can't let that happen.

19:09.781 --> 19:12.284
I'll take the fall, no matter what.

19:15.160 --> 19:18.287
Goodbye, Meg.
I'll always value your friendship.

19:18.788 --> 19:20.789
I love you, Mayor ChapStick.

19:25.127 --> 19:27.796
Brian? What are you doing here?

19:27.921 --> 19:30.798
I just wanted to give you this.

19:31.214 --> 19:33.591
I don't think I'll be needing it anymore.

19:33.717 --> 19:35.928
I got so caught up in
taking down Mayor West

19:36.010 --> 19:38.471
that I just lost sight of right and wrong.

19:39.013 --> 19:41.932
- Thank you, Brian.
- Well, can I give you a lift home?

19:42.015 --> 19:43.142
My cab's right outside.

19:55.945 --> 19:57.903
<i>Good evening. I'm Diane Simmons,</i>

19:58.029 --> 20:01.405
<i>and I'd like to welcome you
to Quahog's Fifth Annual Talent Show.</i>

20:01.489 --> 20:04.284
<i>Let's have a round of applause
for our first performer.</i>

20:10.622 --> 20:12.082
Play me off, Johnny.

20:18.545 --> 20:20.755
<i>What else be funny tonight?</i>

20:20.964 --> 20:23.299
<i>Star Jones got married.
That was in the news.</i>

20:23.424 --> 20:27.845
<i>Married a black fellow, which is quite a
surprise because I'd call her quite a catch.</i>

20:27.928 --> 20:31.722
<i>And black guys, by and large,
they're not so helpful on a fishing vessel.</i>

20:31.847 --> 20:34.349
<i>Now, Portuguese, absolutely, absolutely.</i>

20:34.474 --> 20:37.352
<i>I even had a couple of Japanese guys
who worked out great.</i>

20:37.477 --> 20:40.229
<i>Thank you very much.
You guys have been terrific.</i>

20:41.189 --> 20:44.024
<i>And now, our final performance
of the night.</i>

20:44.191 --> 20:46.818
<i>Let's hear it for Handful of Peter.</i>

21:39.528 --> 21:42.655
I can't believe we lost the talent show.
What'd we do wrong?

21:42.739 --> 21:44.741
Well, Dad, I think I can shed
a little light on that.

21:44.823 --> 21:46.367
You guys were so baked,

21:46.492 --> 21:49.328
you didn't sound anywhere near
as good as you thought you did.

21:49.412 --> 21:50.579
I was in the audience.

22:01.213 --> 22:03.881
And here we thought
the weed was inspiring us.

22:04.007 --> 22:06.383
Well, that's a popular misconception,
Mom and Dad.

22:06.466 --> 22:10.428
But the fact is the chief ingredient
in marijuana is THC,

22:10.595 --> 22:12.012
a mild form of acid,

22:12.095 --> 22:14.723
prolonged usage of which
can cause adverse effects

22:14.807 --> 22:17.392
to your sexual potency,
short-term memory loss,

22:17.517 --> 22:20.271
and can also severely damage
your brain tissue,

22:20.395 --> 22:22.771
central nervous system
and basic motor skills.

22:22.896 --> 22:26.817
To put it simply, Mom and Dad,
there's a reason that they call it dope.

22:27.484 --> 22:29.569
<i>Trying to watch Mr. Belvedere.</i>

22:29.694 --> 22:31.655
So my advice to the two of you would be...

22:31.656 --> 23:32.656
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru